":"Red Cone Spring","kind":"hot spring","lon":-122.18578,"lat":42.99391,"ele_m":null,"wikidata":"Q49732878","url":null},{"id":"node/5560622945","name":"Union Creek Spring","kind":"hot spring","lon":-122.22674,"lat":42.84632,"ele_m":null,"wikidata":"Q49738927","url":null},{"id":"node/2313727652","name":"Annie Falls","kind":"waterfall","lon":-122.11405,"lat":42.81753,"ele_m":1557.0,"wikidata":"Q30625474","url":null,"tour":1,"photos":[],"street":{"image_id":"300633232741096","username":"networklanman","captured_at":"2016-01-22","is_pano":false,"dist_m":130,"url":"https://www.mapillary.com/app/?pKey=300633232741096","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"id":"node/2313760446","name":"Duwee Falls","kind":"waterfall","lon":-122.14726,"lat":42.86455,"ele_m":null,"wikidata":"Q38252250","url":null},{"id":"node/2452430293","name":"Plaikni Falls","kind":"waterfall","lon":-122.04929,"lat":42.90949,"ele_m":null,"wikidata":"Q38251608","url":null},{"id":"node/357332327","name":"Mount Mazama","kind":"peak","lon":-122.10353,"lat":42.93801,"ele_m":null,"wikidata":"Q1201788","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Mazama","tour":4,"summary":{"extract":"Mount Mazama is a complex volcano in the western U.S. state of Oregon, in a segment of the Cascade Volcanic Arc and Cascade Range. The volcano is in Klamath County, in the southern Cascades, 60 miles (97 km) north of the Oregon–California border. Its collapse, due to the eruption of magma emptying the underlying magma chamber, formed a caldera that holds Crater Lake. Mount Mazama originally had an elevation of approximately 12,000 feet (3,700 m), but following its climactic eruption this was reduced to 8,157 feet (2,486 m). Crater Lake is 1,943 feet (592 m) deep, the deepest freshwater body in the United States and the second deepest in North America after Great Slave Lake in Canada.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Mazama","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","attribution":"Wikipedia"},"photos":[{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Mt._Mazama%2C_Crater_Lake_NP%2C_OR_8-13_%2816070571629%29.jpg/960px-Mt._Mazama%2C_Crater_Lake_NP%2C_OR_8-13_%2816070571629%29.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mt._Mazama,_Crater_Lake_NP,_OR_8-13_(16070571629).jpg","dist_m":130,"width":640,"height":776,"license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","artist":"inkknife_2000 (7.5 million views +)"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Greetings_from_Crater_Lake%2C_Oregon_-_Large_Letter_Postcard_%285326938126%29.jpg/960px-Greetings_from_Crater_Lake%2C_Oregon_-_Large_Letter_Postcard_%285326938126%29.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Greetings_from_Crater_Lake,_Oregon_-_Large_Letter_Postcard_(5326938126).jpg","dist_m":246,"width":640,"height":410,"license":"CC BY 2.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","artist":"Steve Shook from Moscow, Idaho, USA"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Crater_Lake_National_Park%2C_OR_2006_%286539570117%29.jpg/960px-Crater_Lake_National_Park%2C_OR_2006_%286539570117%29.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Crater_Lake_National_Park,_OR_2006_(6539570117).jpg","dist_m":298,"width":640,"height":853,"license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","artist":"inkknife_2000 (7.5 million views +)"}],"street":null},{"id":"node/357315268","name":"Mount Scott","kind":"peak","lon":-122.01621,"lat":42.923,"ele_m":2636.0,"wikidata":"Q1507158","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Scott_(Klamath_County,_Oregon)","tour":7,"summary":{"extract":"Mount Scott is a small stratovolcano and a so-called parasitic cone on the southeast flank of Crater Lake in southern Oregon. It is approximately 420,000 years old. Its summit is the highest point within Crater Lake National Park, and the tenth highest peak in the Oregon Cascades.\nA small fire lookout tower stands on the summit, at the end of a trail that zigzags approximately 1,500 feet up the mountain. The mountain is named for Oregon pioneer Levi Scott, founder of Scottsburg, Oregon.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Scott_(Klamath_County%2C_Oregon)","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","attribution":"Wikipedia"},"photos":[{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Crater_Lake_from_Mount_Scott_in_2011_%282%29.JPG/960px-Crater_Lake_from_Mount_Scott_in_2011_%282%29.JPG","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Crater_Lake_from_Mount_Scott_in_2011_(2).JPG","dist_m":203,"width":640,"height":427,"license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","artist":"Chmee2"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Crater_Lake_from_Mount_Scott_in_2011_%283%29.JPG/960px-Crater_Lake_from_Mount_Scott_in_2011_%283%29.JPG","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Crater_Lake_from_Mount_Scott_in_2011_(3).JPG","dist_m":203,"width":640,"height":427,"license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","artist":"Chmee2"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Crater_Lake_from_Mount_Scott_in_2011_%282%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/960px-Crater_Lake_from_Mount_Scott_in_2011_%282%29_%28cropped%29.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Crater_Lake_from_Mount_Scott_in_2011_(2)_(cropped).jpg","dist_m":203,"width":640,"height":320,"license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","artist":"Chmee2 derivative work: User:Maps and stuff (cropped to 2:1 ratio to remove mos…"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Crater_Lake_from_Mount_Scott_in_2011_%284%29.JPG/960px-Crater_Lake_from_Mount_Scott_in_2011_%284%29.JPG","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Crater_Lake_from_Mount_Scott_in_2011_(4).JPG","dist_m":203,"width":640,"height":427,"license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","license_url":"https://creativ